    <bpmn:process id="W_W1637" name="W1637. Vendor Shipping Error &amp; Wrong Item Return Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Goods receipt reveals wrong item, wrong quantity, or wrong specification received
Frequency: ~100–150 shipping errors/month (~2% of GRs)
Volume: ~25–35 per DC/month
Owner: Receiving Clerk
Participants: Receiving Clerk, DC Supervisor, Buyer, AP Clerk
Source: workflow W1637 — Vendor Shipping Error &amp; Wrong Item Return Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1637_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1637_Lane1" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1637_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1637_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1637_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1637_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1637_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1637_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1637_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1637_Start4" name="Goods receipt reveals wrong item, wrong quantity, or wrong specification received">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1637_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1637_Task5" name="At GR: Receiving Clerk identifies shipping error: (a) wrong item received (SKU…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: At GR: Receiving Clerk identifies shipping error: (a) wrong item received (SKU doesn&#x27;t match PO line), (b) wrong quantity (over-shipment or under-shipment), (c) wrong specification (e.g., wrong size, color, grade), (d) damaged in transit (carrier liability — separate from vendor error)
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 5 min/occurrence</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1637_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1637_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1637_Task6" name="Receiving Clerk records discrepancy in system: (a) creates GR discrepancy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Receiving Clerk records discrepancy in system: (a) creates GR discrepancy record with photos, (b) system blocks discrepancy quantity from available stock, (c) notifies Buyer of shipping error
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1637_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1637_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1637_Task7" name="Wrong item">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Buyer contacts vendor to resolve: (a) Wrong item: vendor arranges pickup of wrong items and expedited shipment of correct items; no AP payment for wrong items, (b) Over-shipment: Buyer decides — accept excess (negotiate discount) or return excess per W1631, (c) Under-shipment: vendor ships remaining quantity on expedited basis; PO remains open, (d) Wrong specification: vendor arranges return and replacement; if spec difference is minor and acceptable to BuildRight, Buyer may negotiate price reduction instead
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1637_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1637_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1637_Task8" name="Resolution executed: (a) returns processed per W1631, (b) AP adjusted per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Resolution executed: (a) returns processed per W1631, (b) AP adjusted per W1632, (c) correct items received and processed per standard GR, (d) vendor shipping error rate tracked in vendor scorecard per W44
Responsible (R): Buyer / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Category Manager / Controller
Duration: Variable</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1637_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1637_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1637_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1637_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-338 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Returns &amp; Recovery (PA-32.2).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Receiving Clerk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
